HST Office: Writer outlined every formula and picture on screen with a thin grey line: the
"boundary" it draws around each fly frame while View > Text Boundaries is on (the default).
MathType objects in running text, HST formulas and figures looked boxed, though the line is
neither printed nor exported and Word draws none. Fly frames that show a picture or an
embedded object (OLE: MathType, Equation 3.0, HST formulas, charts) now get no boundary line,
as upstream already did for charts in the frame's own paint. Text frames, sections and tables
keep their boundaries; borders set in the document and the selection handles are unchanged.
The decision lives in HST's sw/source/core/hst/objectboundary.cxx.

