+class SwLayoutFrame;
+
+namespace sw::hst
+{
+/// Whether the layout frame is a fly frame that shows a picture or an embedded object (a MathType
+/// or HST formula, a chart, any OLE object) instead of text. Such a frame gets no on-screen
+/// boundary line: the object is its own visual extent, as in Word, where neither pictures nor
+/// equations are outlined. Text frames, sections and tables keep their boundaries, and borders
+/// set in the document are painted as before.
+bool IsPictureOrObjectFly(const SwLayoutFrame& rFrame);
+}
